+    # A SUB WITHOUT A SIGNATURE STILL TAKES ARGUMENTS, and its arity is not on
+    # the wire. `sub f { my $n = shift }` ships a signature record of
+    # kind=implicit holding the SLURPY `@_` -- which is not a positional, so
+    # the declared list is empty, while the sub plainly takes one argument.
+    # `sub lit { return (10,20,30) }` ships the SAME record and takes none.
+    # The signature cannot tell them apart because neither HAS one; the
+    # difference is in the body, in whether it reads `@_`.
